{"name":"Warm Turbulence","hex":"#f3f5dc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"warm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a somewhat high temperature, often but not always connoting that the high temperature is pleasant rather than uncomfortable.","Friendly and with affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make or keep warm.","To become warm, to heat up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warm"},{"term":"turbulence","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state or fact of being turbulent or agitated; tempestuousness, disturbance.","Disturbance in a gas or fluid, characterized by evidence of internal motion or unrest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turbulence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Turbulence","blocks":[{"text":"In fluid dynamics, turbulence or turbulent flow is fluid motion exhibiting chaotic changes in pressure and flow velocity. It is in contrast to laminar flow, which occurs when a fluid flows in parallel layers with no disruption between those layers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turbulence","wikidata":"Q190132"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Los_Angeles_attack_sub_2.jpg/500px-Los_Angeles_attack_sub_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Los_Angeles_attack_sub_2.jpg/500px-Los_Angeles_attack_sub_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Laminar and turbulent water flow over the hull of a submarine. As the relative velocity of the water increases, turbulence occurs.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALos_Angeles_attack_sub_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg/500px-Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg/1280px-Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg/500px-Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Turbulence in the tip vortex from an airplane wing passing through coloured smoke ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAirplane_vortex_edit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/False_color_image_of_the_far_field_of_a_submerged_turbulent_jet.jpg/330px-False_color_image_of_the_far_field_of_a_submerged_turbulent_jet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/False_color_image_of_the_far_field_of_a_submerged_turbulent_jet.jpg/330px-False_color_image_of_the_far_field_of_a_submerged_turbulent_jet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flow visualization of a turbulent jet, made by laser-induced fluorescence. The jet exhibits a wide range of length scales, an important characteristic of turbulent flows.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFalse_color_image_of_the_far_field_of_a_submerged_turbulent_jet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Laminar-turbulent_transition.jpg/500px-Laminar-turbulent_transition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Laminar-turbulent_transition.jpg/1280px-Laminar-turbulent_transition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Laminar-turbulent_transition.jpg/500px-Laminar-turbulent_transition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The plume from this candle flame goes from laminar to turbulent. The Reynolds number can be used to predict where this transition will take place","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALaminar-turbulent_transition.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/MIT_2.22_Design_Principles_for_Ocean_Vehicles_%2813.42%29%2C_Spring_2005_-_Design_Principles_for_Ocean_Vehicles_%2813.42%29_-_4150121031.jpg/500px-MIT_2.22_Design_Principles_for_Ocean_Vehicles_%2813.42%29%2C_Spring_2005_-_Design_Principles_for_Ocean_Vehicles_%2813.42%29_-_4150121031.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/MIT_2.22_Design_Principles_for_Ocean_Vehicles_%2813.42%29%2C_Spring_2005_-_Design_Principles_for_Ocean_Vehicles_%2813.42%29_-_4150121031.jpg/500px-MIT_2.22_Design_Principles_for_Ocean_Vehicles_%2813.42%29%2C_Spring_2005_-_Design_Principles_for_Ocean_Vehicles_%2813.42%29_-_4150121031.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reynolds number dependency. From top to bottom: regime of unseparated flow; a fixed pair of Foppl vortices in the wake; two laminar vortex street regimes; transition to turbulent vortex street; laminar boundary layer transitions to turbulence, disorganized wake; re-establishment of turbulent vortex …","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMIT_2.22_Design_Principles_for_Ocean_Vehicles_(13.42)%2C_Spring_2005_-_Design_Principles_for_Ocean_Vehicles_(13.42)_-_4150121031.jpg"}],"sounds":{"warm":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/En-us-warm.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/36/En-us-warm.ogg/En-us-warm.ogg.mp3"}],"turbulence":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/43/LL-Q1860_%28e